      "type": "A",
      "evidence": "as appropriate",
      "rewrite": "upon generation or as mandated by regulations"
    },
    {
      "type": "V",
      "evidence": "in order to comply with the applicable fishing regulations",
      "rewrite": "to ensure compliance, reports must be transmitted to ERS within 24 hours of creation, with confirmation logs maintained for verification."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "item": "R1",
  "scores": {"U": 2, "A": 2, "C": 3, "V": 1},
  "confidences": {"U": 0.9, "A": 0.95, "C": 0.8, "V": 0.98},
  "rationales": {"U":"'All electr onic reports' contains typographical errors ('electr onic', 'transmit ted', 'Syste m', 'regu lations') that impair readability and suggest unreviewed drafting; 'as appropriate' is vague and undermines clarity about scope and applicability", "A":"'as appropriate' introduces ambiguity — it is undefined which reports are 'appropriate' to transmit, and under what conditions; 'UK fisheries administrations' is plural but ERS is singular, creating uncertainty about responsible authority", "C":"The requirement aligns broadly with UK fishing regulation intent, but 'applicable fishing regu lations' is misspelled and lacks reference to specific statutory instruments (e.g., The Sea Fishing (Electronic Recording and Reporting) Regulations 2022), reducing traceability to legal basis", "V":"No testable criteria are provided: no defined report types, no transmission timing (e.g., 'within 2 hours of landing'), no format constraints (e.g., XML schema v1.2), no success/failure indicators (e.g., 'ERS must return HTTP 201 with receipt ID'), making objective verification impossible"},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace with: 'All electronic reports generated by UK fishing vessels — including catch returns, landing declarations, and transhipment notifications — must be transmitted to the UK Fisheries Administration’s Electronic Recording and Reporting System (ERS)'", "A":"Replace with: 'Each electronic report listed in Annex A (Report Types) must be transmitted to the UK Fisheries Administration’s ERS within 2 hours of report generation, without exception'", "C":"Replace with: 'This requirement implements Regulation 5(1) of The Sea Fishing (Electronic Recording and Reporting) Regulations 2022 (SI 2022/1043)'", "V":"Replace with: 'The vessel’s ERS client software shall transmit each report in ISO/IEC 11179-compliant XML format (schema version ERS-XML-2.1), using TLS 1.2+, and shall log the ERS response code (e.g., 201 Created) and timestamped receipt ID within 5 seconds of transmission completion'"}, 
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"All electr onic reports from UK fishing vessels are required to be transmit ted to the Electronic Recording and Reporting Syste m (ERS) of the UK fisheries administrations as appropriate","rewrite":"All electronic reports generated by UK fishing vessels — including catch returns, landing declarations, and transhipment notifications — must be transmitted to the UK Fisheries Administration’s Electronic Recording and Reporting System (ERS)"},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"as appropriate","rewrite":"Each electronic report listed in Annex A (Report Types) must be transmitted to the UK Fisheries Administration’s ERS within 2 hours of report generation, without exception"},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"are required to be transmit ted to the Electronic Recording and Reporting Syste m (ERS) of the UK fisheries administrations as appropriate in order to comply with the applicable fishing regu lations","rewrite":"The vessel’s ERS client software shall transmit each report in ISO/IEC 11179-compliant XML format (schema version ERS-XML-2.1), using TLS 1.2+, and shall log the ERS response code (e.g., 201 Created) and timestamped receipt ID within 5 seconds of transmission completion"}
  ]
}
